Z||000012||fieroshop||05-24-2000||01:14 AM||||For those of you wondering if that is a Fiero yellow (Hey it rhymes, Guess I'm a poet and didn't know it) That 87 GT was silver and we painted it here at the Fiero Shop. Wait till you see my 88 GT We are preping the GT now and it should be btter yet it will be ready for the Poker run. I want one of those trophies, yea! yea! I know, you guys say just make one, but it would not be the same as actually winning one even if I do make them.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Robert||05-25-2000||09:26 PM||||BOY….  Go away for a few days in Santa Barbara, and look what I miss.   Yes, that’s my Yellow 87GT.  George painted it with 88 Fiero/Corvette yellow, with a little red tint thrown in to make it unique.  It has at least 3 coats of yellow followed by 3 coats of clear.  Sunglasses must be worn by anyone within thirty feet.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <BR>We’ll be at the poker run again this year, I only hope I pick a better hand than last year.<P>See ya later all<P>Robert <BR>||||reg||10
